From: SM-X710 postmarketOS port <gts9wifi@example.com>
Date: Sun, 20 Sep 2026 04:00:00 +0300
Subject: [PATCH] remoteproc: qcom_q6v5: stop logging a repeated handover interrupt

The ADSP handover interrupt is level-triggered: the remote processor keeps it
asserted after the first handover, so q6v5_handover_interrupt() takes the
already-issued branch again for the rest of the session.  On the SM-X710 it
repeats about 5.4 times a second.

Measured on this port's own tablet (2026-09-26, Fedora issue 19): 37,402 of
37,411 lines in the dmesg ring were this one message - 99.98 % - so every real
diagnostic was evicted from the ring within seconds of being logged.  That
includes the lines the stall investigation needs, and it makes `dmesg` useless
as an evidence source without an out-of-band filter.

The repeat is expected and harmless: the handover has already been performed by
the time it arrives.  Log it at debug level so it cannot flood the log.  The
interrupt is still handled exactly as before, so there is no behaviour change.

Origin: troikoss/gts9wifi-fedora, kernel/patches/
quiet-adsp-handover-already-happened.patch.  Taken here because this port
enables the same ADSP remoteproc (CONFIG_QCOM_Q6V5_PAS=y, `&remoteproc_adsp`
status = "okay") and hits the same level-triggered repeat.

Signed-off-by: SM-X710 mainline port <gts9wifi@example.com>
diff --git a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
index 58d5b85e5..9c189428b 100644
--- a/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
+++ b/drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5.c
@@ -165,7 +165,15 @@ static irqreturn_t q6v5_handover_interrupt(int irq, void *data)
 	struct qcom_q6v5 *q6v5 = data;
 
 	if (q6v5->handover_issued) {
-		dev_err(q6v5->dev, "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
+		/*
+		 * The handover interrupt is level-triggered and the remote keeps
+		 * it asserted after the first handover, so this branch is taken
+		 * again and again (about five times a second on the SM-X710) and
+		 * buries the rest of the kernel log.  The handover itself has
+		 * already happened, so log the repeat at debug level instead of
+		 * at error level.
+		 */
+		dev_dbg(q6v5->dev, "Handover signaled, but it already happened\n");
 		return IRQ_HANDLED;
 	}
 
